From: Gaurav Suman <gauravsuman007@gmail.com>

Add a V4L2 sub-device driver for the Samsung S5KGD1 32MP quad-Bayer
sensor. It supports the 2x2 binned 3264x2448 RAW10 mode at 30 fps on
four CSI-2 lanes at 761.6 Mbps per lane, from a 19.2 MHz MCLK, with
exposure, analogue gain, vertical blanking and test pattern controls.

The register settings come from the LG G8x ThinQ vendor camera
module data (com.qti.sensormodule.s5kgd1_front.bin). The
initialisation sequence is long (5474 writes, mostly a firmware patch
through the indirect 0x6028/0x602a/0x6f12 window) and is written at
every stream start.

Tested on an LG G8x ThinQ (SM8150, CSIPHY2).

This was written and tested with the help of an AI coding assistant
(Claude Opus 5.5, Anthropic); I reviewed the change and the results.

Signed-off-by: Gaurav Suman <gauravsuman007@gmail.com>
